rca of the issue:
File /app/frontend/src/pages/student/TryoutEngine.js lines 46-49:
```
const [fontStep, setFontStep] = useState(() => {
  const v = Number(localStorage.getItem('exam_font_step'));
  return Number.isInteger(v) && v >= 0 && v < FONT_STEPS.length ? v : 1;
});
```
When `exam_font_step` is missing, `localStorage.getItem` returns `null`. `Number(null)` evaluates to `0` (not `NaN`), and `Number.isInteger(0)` is `true`, with `0 >= 0 && 0 < 5` also true. So the guard admits 0 and the state defaults to `FONT_STEPS[0] = 0.9` (=90%) instead of the fallback `1` (=100%). Mitigation: null-check the raw value first, e.g. `const raw = localStorage.getItem('exam_font_step'); const v = raw === null ? NaN : Number(raw);` — then the existing isInteger guard will correctly fall through to the default `1`.
